1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,613
One drop of food colouring is placed gently into a beaker of cold water and another into a beaker of hot water.

2
00:00:06,613 --> 00:00:12,281
Nobody stirs them. Predict: in which beaker will the colour spread out faster? Pause and decide.

3
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:17,650
Watch. After one minute the colour has started to spread in both beakers.

4
00:00:18,709 --> 00:00:22,251
After five minutes the hot water is almost evenly coloured,

5
00:00:22,251 --> 00:00:25,971
but in the cold water the colour is still mostly in the middle.

6
00:00:27,030 --> 00:00:28,329
Explain what you saw.

7
00:00:28,329 --> 00:00:36,004
The colour spreads by diffusion: its particles move randomly and spread from where there are many of them to where there are few.

8
00:00:36,004 --> 00:00:41,672
In hot water the particles have more energy and move faster, so diffusion happens more quickly.

9
00:00:41,672 --> 00:00:43,975
Pause and explain it in your own words.

10
00:00:45,034 --> 00:00:49,580
Spray perfume in one corner of a room, and soon you can smell it everywhere.

11
00:00:49,580 --> 00:00:54,126
This is diffusion: particles of one substance spreading out through another,

12
00:00:54,126 --> 00:00:58,141
from an area of high concentration to an area of low concentration.

13
00:00:58,141 --> 00:01:01,625
It happens on its own, because particles are always moving.

14
00:01:02,684 --> 00:01:07,997
Diffusion happens in liquids and gases, where particles move freely and collide randomly.

15
00:01:07,997 --> 00:01:09,414
Put a tea bag in water,

16
00:01:09,414 --> 00:01:14,846
and the tea particles slowly spread out until they're evenly mixed with the water particles.

17
00:01:15,905 --> 00:01:20,865
Diffusion is faster when the particles are lighter, when the temperature is higher,

18
00:01:20,865 --> 00:01:27,123
and when there are bigger spaces between particles. That's why it's much faster in gases than in liquids.

19
00:01:27,123 --> 00:01:30,016
Remember, diffusion isn't the same as dissolving!

20
00:01:31,075 --> 00:01:36,566
Now it is your turn to shine! Pause the video after each question and try to answer it first.

21
00:01:37,625 --> 00:01:43,175
Question 1: A box weighing 600 newtons rests on 2 square metres. What pressure does it exert?

22
00:01:43,175 --> 00:01:44,356
Pause the video now.

23
00:01:45,415 --> 00:01:46,773
Answer: 300 newtons/m².

24
00:01:47,832 --> 00:01:53,500
Question 2: Why does water spurt furthest from the lowest hole in a bottle? Pause the video now.

25
00:01:54,559 --> 00:01:56,802
Answer: Pressure increases with depth.

26
00:01:57,861 --> 00:02:03,884
Question 3: What happens to gas pressure in a sealed container when it is heated? Pause the video now.

27
00:02:04,943 --> 00:02:08,544
Answer: It increases, particles move faster and collide more.

28
00:02:09,603 --> 00:02:14,976
Question 4: Why does diffusion happen faster in gases than in liquids? Pause the video now.

29
00:02:16,035 --> 00:02:20,168
Answer: Gas particles move faster and have bigger spaces between them.
